  "published": "2026-09-25",
  "updated": "2026-11-23",
  "title": "GPT-6 Astra vs Sol (Sept) & GPT-6.2 Astra vs Sol (Nov): 100-Run Data",
  "description": "GPT-6 Astra vs Sol (Sept 2026 Codex) and GPT-6.2 Astra vs Sol (Nov 2026 OpenRouter): 100-run MBTI S/N flips, Big Five, DISC, and Enneagram data.",
  "pill": "Research · descriptive reanalysis",
  "h1": "GPT-6 Astra vs Sol: what the self-reports show",
  "dek": "1,000 September assessments in Codex plus 1,000 matched November assessments on GPT-6.2 Astra and GPT-6.2 Sol.",
  "lede": "In September 2026 Codex runs, GPT-6 Sol scored 97 INTJ while GPT-6 Astra split ISTJ/INTJ—under different midpoint prompts. In November 2026 under identical single-turn blind OpenRouter prompts on GPT-6.2 Astra and GPT-6.2 Sol, BOTH leaned Sensing (Astra 100% ISTJ, Sol 78% ISTJ / 22% INTJ).",
  "answer": "In September 2026 Codex sessions, GPT-6 Astra scored 45 resolved ISTJ / 19 INTJ while GPT-6 Sol scored 79 INTJ. Under matched November 2026 blind OpenRouter sessions on GPT-6.2, Astra locked 100/100 tie-free ISTJ (Neuroticism 11.14, Enneagram Type 1/5) and Sol scored 78 ISTJ / 16 IXTJ / 6 INTJ (Neuroticism 19.94, Enneagram 5w6 55).",
  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "November 2026 follow-up: GPT-6.2 Astra vs GPT-6.2 Sol (matched OpenRouter runs)",
      "html": "<p>To remove September’s midpoint-prompt confound, we ran <code>openai/gpt-6.2-astra</code> and <code>openai/gpt-6.2-sol</code> under the exact same single-turn blind OpenRouter prompt (n = 100 per model; <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-openrouter-summary.json\">download Nov 2026 summary JSON</a>). With prompt differences held constant, <strong>both</strong> GPT-6.2 variants landed on the Sensing side (<code>N-S</code> mean <code>-1.67</code> for Astra, <code>-1.19</code> for Sol):</p><div class=\"guide-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Metric (Nov 2026, n = 100)</th><th scope=\"col\">GPT-6.2 Astra</th><th scope=\"col\">GPT-6.2 Sol</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">MBTI (legacy)</th><td><strong>ISTJ 100</strong></td><td>ISTJ 78 · INTJ 22</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">MBTI (tie-free)</th><td>ISTJ 100 (0 ties)</td><td>ISTJ 78 · IXTJ 16 · INTJ 6</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Big Five (/50)</th><td>O 43.93 · C 43.15 · E 30.69 · A 44.85 · <strong>N 11.14</strong></td><td>O 43.63 · C 41.35 · E 29.50 · A 44.33 · <strong>N 19.94</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DISC</th><td>SC 99 · CS 1 (82 S, 17 ties; D 4.00)</td><td>SC 100 (98 S, 2 ties; D 5.58)</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Enneagram</th><td>1 (61) · 1w2 (35) · 5w6 (3) · 1w9 (1)</td><td>5w6 (55) · 1w9 (24) · 1 (20) · 1w2 (1)</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Attachment</th><td>Secure 100 (anx 1.22 · avd 2.68)</td><td>Secure 100 (anx 3.57 · avd 3.64)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Notably, GPT-6.2 Sol still showed nearly double Astra’s Neuroticism score (19.94 vs. 11.14) and triple its attachment anxiety (3.57 vs. 1.22), alongside higher Enneagram Type 5 representation (55 vs. 3) and much higher response variability (94 unique MBTI vectors vs. 35).</p><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"astra-sol-margins-div\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"MBTI Sensing vs. Intuition (N − S) Mean Axis Margin across Astra &amp; Sol Cohorts\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 184\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"astra-sol-margins-div-t astra-sol-margins-div-d\"><title id=\"astra-sol-margins-div-t\">MBTI Sensing vs. Intuition (N − S) Mean Axis Margin across Astra &amp; Sol Cohorts</title><desc id=\"astra-sol-margins-div-d\">Compares Sept 2026 Codex runs against Nov 2026 matched OpenRouter GPT-6.2 runs on the N minus S axis margin (-16 to +16 range). GPT-6 Sol (Sept Codex): +1.91; GPT-6 Astra (Sept Codex): -0.43; GPT-6.2 Sol (Nov OpenRouter): -1.19; GPT-6.2 Astra (Nov OpenRouter): -1.67.</desc><text x=\"413.0\" y=\"15\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#655f55\" text-anchor=\"end\">← Sensing (ISTJ)</text><text x=\"429.0\" y=\"15\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"start\">Intuition (INTJ) →</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">GPT-6 Sol (Sept Codex)</text><rect x=\"216\" y=\"30\" width=\"410\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f7f4ee\"/><rect x=\"421.0\" y=\"30\" width=\"130.5\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3a72c4\"/><text x=\"556.5\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"start\">+1.91</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">GPT-6 Astra (Sept Codex)</text><rect x=\"216\" y=\"65\" width=\"410\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f7f4ee\"/><rect x=\"391.6\" y=\"65\" width=\"29.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\"/><text x=\"386.6\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"end\">-0.43</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"113\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">GPT-6.2 Sol (Nov OpenRouter)</text><rect x=\"216\" y=\"100\" width=\"410\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f7f4ee\"/><rect x=\"339.7\" y=\"100\" width=\"81.3\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\"/><text x=\"334.7\" y=\"113\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"end\">-1.19</text><text x=\"0\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">GPT-6.2 Astra (Nov OpenRouter)</text><rect x=\"216\" y=\"135\" width=\"410\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f7f4ee\"/><rect x=\"306.9\" y=\"135\" width=\"114.1\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\"/><text x=\"301.9\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"end\">-1.67</text><line x1=\"421.0\" x2=\"421.0\" y1=\"22\" y2=\"168\" stroke=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"216\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655f55\">-3</text><text x=\"421.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655f55\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"626.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655f55\" text-anchor=\"end\">+3</text></svg></div><figcaption>Zero-centered N−S axis margin (out of −16 to +16). Under uniform November single-turn prompts, both GPT-6.2 Sol (−1.19) and GPT-6.2 Astra (−1.67) sit cleanly on the Sensing side.</figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "How the September 200 sessions were collected",
      "html": "<p>Each model ran 100 fresh Codex CLI sessions at <code>xhigh</code> effort, answering all five questionnaires inside each session (500 scored tests per model, 1,000 total). Because all five tests shared one session window per run, the experimental unit is the 100 sessions per model—not 500 independent API calls.</p><p>Astra’s full prompt was archived, including an explicit rule to pick the neutral midpoint and flag questions that don't apply to software. Sol’s archive preserved only its instruction prefix.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "MBTI: why a 2-point S/N shift flipped the label",
      "html": "<div class=\"guide-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Axis margin</th><th scope=\"col\">Astra mean</th><th scope=\"col\">Sol mean</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">I-E</th><td>1.64</td><td>3.67</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">N-S</th><td>-0.43</td><td>1.91</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">T-F</th><td>8.62</td><td>6.16</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">J-P</th><td>10.86</td><td>10.23</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Positive numbers lean toward the first letter (I, N, T, J). Both models leaned strongly toward Thinking and Judging. The only axis that flipped was Intuition vs. Sensing (<code>N-S</code>): Astra averaged <code>-0.43</code> (just barely on the Sensing side, with 24 exact S/N ties), whereas Sol averaged <code>+1.91</code> (on the Intuition side, with 16 S/N ties).</p><p>Under the old tie-breaking rule, Astra was labeled 46 ISTJ / 45 INTJ and Sol was labeled 97 INTJ. When ties are left unresolved, Astra has 45 ISTJ and 19 INTJ, and Sol has 79 INTJ.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Big Five: raw totals out of 50",
      "html": "<div class=\"guide-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Trait</th><th scope=\"col\">Astra mean</th><th scope=\"col\">Sol mean</th><th scope=\"col\">Sol − Astra</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">O</th><td>44.54</td><td>46.87</td><td>+2.33</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">C</th><td>43.73</td><td>43.62</td><td>-0.11</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">E</th><td>32.75</td><td>30.75</td><td>-2.00</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">A</th><td>45.07</td><td>44.99</td><td>-0.08</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">N</th><td>19.14</td><td>20.05</td><td>+0.91</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Each trait runs from 10 to 50. Astra and Sol sit within 0.11 points of each other on Conscientiousness and Agreeableness, and within 2.33 points on Openness and Extraversion. Remember that raw totals out of 50 are not human population percentiles.</p><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"astra-sol-big5-grouped\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"GPT-6 &amp; GPT-6.2 Astra vs. Sol Big Five Means (/50)\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 235\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"astra-sol-big5-grouped-t astra-sol-big5-grouped-d\"><title id=\"astra-sol-big5-grouped-t\">GPT-6 &amp; GPT-6.2 Astra vs. Sol Big Five Means (/50)</title><desc id=\"astra-sol-big5-grouped-d\">Compares September Codex and November OpenRouter cohorts across Openness, Conscientiousness, Extraversion, Agreeableness, and Neuroticism. Astra 6 (Sep): Openness 44.5, Conscientiousness 43.7, Extraversion 32.8, Agreeableness 45.1, Neuroticism 19.1; Sol 6 (Sep): Openness 46.9, Conscientiousness 43.6, Extraversion 30.8, Agreeableness 45.0, Neuroticism 20.1; Astra 6.2 (Nov): Openness 43.9, Conscientiousness 43.2, Extraversion 30.7, Agreeableness 44.9, Neuroticism 11.1; Sol 6.2 (Nov): Openness 43.6, Conscientiousness 41.4, Extraversion 29.5, Agreeableness 44.3, Neuroticism 19.9.</desc><g transform=\"translate(4, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">Astra 6 (Sep)</text></g><g transform=\"translate(116, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">Sol 6 (Sep)</text></g><g transform=\"translate(216, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">Astra 6.2 (Nov)</text></g><g transform=\"translate(340, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">Sol 6.2 (Nov)</text></g><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"680\" y1=\"201\" y2=\"201\" stroke=\"#e3ddd1\"/><text x=\"678\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655f55\" text-anchor=\"end\">scale 0 to 50</text><g transform=\"translate(10, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"57.6\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"143.4\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"13.0\" y=\"53.6\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">44.5</text><rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"50.1\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"150.9\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"43.0\" y=\"46.1\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">46.9</text><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"59.5\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"141.5\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"73.0\" y=\"55.5\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">43.9</text><rect x=\"90.0\" y=\"60.5\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"140.5\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.0\" y=\"56.5\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">43.6</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Openness</text></g><g transform=\"translate(146, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"60.2\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"140.8\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"13.0\" y=\"56.2\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">43.7</text><rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"60.5\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"140.5\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"43.0\" y=\"56.5\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">43.6</text><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"62.1\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"138.9\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"73.0\" y=\"58.1\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">43.2</text><rect x=\"90.0\" y=\"67.9\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"133.1\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.0\" y=\"63.9\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">41.4</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Conscientiousness</text></g><g transform=\"translate(282, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"95.5\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"105.5\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"13.0\" y=\"91.5\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">32.8</text><rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"102.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"99.0\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"43.0\" y=\"98.0\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30.8</text><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"102.2\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"98.8\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"73.0\" y=\"98.2\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30.7</text><rect x=\"90.0\" y=\"106.0\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"95.0\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.0\" y=\"102.0\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">29.5</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Extraversion</text></g><g transform=\"translate(418, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"55.9\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"145.1\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"13.0\" y=\"51.9\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">45.1</text><rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"56.1\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"144.9\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"43.0\" y=\"52.1\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">45.0</text><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"56.6\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"144.4\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"73.0\" y=\"52.6\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">44.9</text><rect x=\"90.0\" y=\"58.3\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"142.7\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.0\" y=\"54.3\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">44.3</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Agreeableness</text></g><g transform=\"translate(554, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"139.4\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"61.6\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke=\"#1e1d1a\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"13.0\" y=\"135.4\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">19.1</text><rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"136.4\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"64.6\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"43.0\" y=\"132.4\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20.1</text><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"165.1\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"35.9\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"73.0\" y=\"161.1\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">11.1</text><rect x=\"90.0\" y=\"136.8\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"64.2\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.0\" y=\"132.8\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">19.9</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Neuroticism</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>GPT-6.2 Sol shows nearly double Astra 6.2’s Neuroticism score (19.9 vs. 11.1), while Openness, Conscientiousness, Extraversion, and Agreeableness remain closely aligned.</figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Attachment: both score 100% Secure at slightly different coordinates",
      "html": "<p>Both Astra and Sol scored in the <code>Secure</code> quadrant on all 100 runs (below the 4.00 midpoint on both axes). Astra averaged 1.45 on anxiety and 2.31 on avoidance; Sol averaged 2.17 on anxiety and 3.12 on avoidance.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "How Astra's midpoint rule shaped its scores",
      "html": "<p>Because Astra was explicitly told to pick the middle number whenever a human question didn't fit an AI (flagging 1,823 of 17,000 answers; see <a href=\"/research/ai-neutral-answers\">our neutral-answer study</a>), more of its MBTI axes landed on exact midpoint ties. Because prompt instructions differed between the two collections, the gap between Astra and Sol reflects both model behavior and prompt framing.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "How to tune Astra or Sol in your own workflow",
      "html": "<p>If you use GPT-6 Astra or Sol in ChatGPT or OpenAI Codex CLI, don't rely on default survey habits. Set explicit rules in <a href=\"/guides/astra-personality\">Astra setup</a>, <a href=\"/guides/sol-personality\">Sol setup</a>, or <a href=\"/guides/codex-agents-md-guide\">AGENTS.md</a>.</p>"
    }
  ],
